  "explicit_non_claims": [
    "The oracle is exact only inside the declared path, resource, rate and state-space bounds.",
    "An over-budget instance is unsupported; it is never truncated and presented as exact.",
    "Maximum-sum throughput is not the universally correct objective and may starve a path.",
    "The weighted max-min allocator remains a distinct fairness objective and is not replaced by the oracle.",
    "The oracle is not a production scheduler and must not be called on the packet-forwarding fast path.",
    "A unit-tested integer witness is not measured network behavior.",
    "Resource identities and capacities must already be supplied by the capacity-evidence gate.",
    "No claim of outperforming CAKE, fq_codel, Linux MPTCP, LIA, OLIA or BALIA is made."
  ]
